course: dictionary
lesson: 13021
title: Fabricated: made up or made
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have two meanings, and the sentence tells you which one you need. Read the words around the word: «The newspaper story was fabricated; none of it was true.» The clues are story and true, so fabricated means made up to trick people.
explain: The second meaning is about making things. «The factory fabricated steel beams for the new bridge.» Factory and beams are the clues, so fabricated means made or built from parts.
explain: Always check by swapping your meaning into the sentence. Does "made up to trick people" fit? Does "made or built from parts" fit? The one that makes sense is the right meaning.
fact: Fabricated is the past tense and past participle of fabricate.
fact: «Fabricated» can mean false, made up to trick people: «a fabricated story» is a lie made to look true.
fact: «Fabricated» can also mean made or built, often in a factory from parts: «fabricated steel».
fact: Some sources are fabricated, so historians check where their information came from.
exercise: «The newspaper story was fabricated to fool its readers.» What does fabricated mean here? | *Made up to trick people | Printed in colour | Read out loud on the radio | Carefully checked and approved
exercise: «The workers fabricated the metal frames in the workshop.» What does fabricated mean here? | *Made or built from parts | Broken into small pieces | Painted bright red | Told as a lie
exercise: «She gave a fabricated excuse for being late.» What does fabricated suggest? | *Made up and not true | Very long and detailed | Given in writing | Honest and true
test: «The history teacher asked us to check whether the letter was fabricated.» What does this suggest? | The letter was written in gold ink | *The letter might be false | The letter was made of steel | The letter was very old and valuable
test: Which sentence uses fabricated to mean made or built? | «Her fabricated smile looked fake.» | «The story was fabricated to fool the town.» | *«The engineers fabricated the pipes in their workshop.»
exam: In «Pupils learn to check sources because some are fabricated», what does fabricated mean? | Written in gold ink | Carefully checked and approved | Brand new and never used | *Made up and false
